47. An RFI shall consider the following, amongst others, in assessing the severity of
estimated funding gaps or shortfalls and determining the appropriate
management actions:

a) Size and timing of the funding gap, relative to total funding;

b) The level of actual stress (whether RFI-specific or market-wide) relative to

the modelled level of stress;

c) The level and diversity of funding sources available to meet that shortfall;

and

d) Size of the stock of unencumbered HQLA to meet that shortfall.

